# French Suite No. 5 in G major, BWV 816: Courante (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: an Italian-style corrente rather than a French courante:
# running sixteenths over a walking eighth-note bass, bright and
# forward-moving in 3/4, one beat to the quarter. It should run, but
# lightly; the sixteenth figures are broken chords and need to be heard
# as harmony.
#
# Time signature: 3/4, 32 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI,
# with a sixteenth upbeat (bar 16 is short by that sixteenth, which is
# the upbeat to the second half). The MIDI plays each half once.
#
# Repeats: both halves repeated, written out with play (the first half
# from its upbeat, the second from its upbeat). About 6 KB with repeats.
#   Performed bars: A first time 1-16.92, A repeat 16.92-32.92
#   (score bar x is bar x+16), B first time 32.92-48.92 (score x is
#   x+16), B repeat 48.92-64.92 (score x is x+32).
#
# Tempo: quarter = 116, 64 bars with repeats, about 1:40.
# Track times: Angela Hewitt (Hyperion) 1:37, about quarter = 119 if she
# takes both repeats, as she normally does in the suites; Alessandra
# Artifoni 1:49, about 106 with repeats; Glenn Gould (Sony) 1:16, which
# would be about 150 with repeats, or a slow 76 without, so his repeat
# plan is uncertain and I set it aside. 116 sits just under Hewitt:
# sixteenths are about 7.8 frames each on the chip, clear but running.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score, no published bar-by-bar
# analysis consulted):
#   1-8     G major, the running figure in the right hand over a walking
#           bass; cadence in G at bar 8.
#   9-16    E minor, then A, to a cadence in D major at the end of A.
#   17-20   D major, the figure in the bass, turning to E minor.
#   21-24   E minor, held suspensions in the upper voices over the bass;
#           cadence in E minor (24).
#   25-28   sequence back through A minor and D.
#   29-32   G major, the closing sequence and the final cadence.
#
# Plan: as on a two-manual harpsichord, each half full the first time
# and echoed on the repeat. In the second half the E minor suspensions
# (21-24) are a step down from the bright D major opening; the final
# repeat comes back to full at the closing sequence (score 29).

pickup 16

tempo 116

play 0.916667-16.916667 0.916667-16.916667 16.916667-32.916667 16.916667-32

dyn 1 f            # A, first time (and its upbeat)
dyn 16.916667 mp   # A repeat, an echo
dyn 32.916667 f    # B first time: D major, the figure in the bass
lead 33-34 bottom  # score 17-18: the bass takes the running figure
dyn 37 mf          # score 21-24: E minor suspensions, a step down
dyn 41 f           # score 25-32: sequence home and the close
broaden 48 0.95    # score 32: a breath before the B repeat
dyn 48.916667 mp   # B repeat, an echo
dyn 61 f           # score 29 on: full again for the close

rit 2 0.8          # the last two bars into the final G
